      "problem": "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing simple harmonic motion?",
      "worked_solution": "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\n$$",
